{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>וַיִּגְמֹל שְׁקֵדִים.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 18:23) the reason for almonds — to signal that the punishment of anyone who challenges the priesthood comes swiftly; thus far. And it appears that they were compelled to say this, for it is not fitting for the master of the miracle to seek a fruit that sprouts quickly, which would look, Heaven forbid, like a diminution of His power — that He seeks a fruit that is fast. Therefore they said that there is a reason in the matter, that it was necessary to sprout almonds and no other fruit, to say that He is swift to recompense, etc., for otherwise He would have produced a carob."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:44.393663438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}